<p>On-page SEO is the foundation of every high-ranking website. Before you publish any page — whether it's a blog post, service page or landing page — run through this 25-point checklist. It takes less than 15 minutes and can make the difference between ranking on page 1 or page 5.</p>

<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432888498266-38ffec3eaf0a?w=900&q=80&fit=crop" alt="SEO analytics and keyword research" class="rounded-2xl w-full my-8 shadow-md" loading="lazy" />

<h2>Section 1: Keyword Targeting (5 Points)</h2>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Primary keyword identified</strong> — every page targets one main keyword with clear search intent.</li>
  <li><strong>Keyword in title tag</strong> — your primary keyword appears near the beginning of the title tag.</li>
  <li><strong>Keyword in URL slug</strong> — the URL is short, readable and contains the primary keyword (e.g. /local-seo-guide-kenya).</li>
  <li><strong>Keyword in H1</strong> — the H1 heading (there should be only one per page) contains the primary keyword naturally.</li>
  <li><strong>Keyword in first 100 words</strong> — the primary keyword appears in the opening paragraph.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Section 2: Title Tags and Meta Descriptions (4 Points)</h2>

<ol start="6">
  <li><strong>Title tag length</strong> — between 50–60 characters. Google truncates anything longer in search results.</li>
  <li><strong>Unique title tag</strong> — no two pages on your site share the same title.</li>
  <li><strong>Meta description written</strong> — 150–160 characters, includes primary keyword and a clear reason to click.</li>
  <li><strong>No duplicate meta descriptions</strong> — every page has a unique meta description.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Section 3: Headings and Content Structure (4 Points)</h2>

<ol start="10">
  <li><strong>One H1 only</strong> — each page has exactly one H1 tag.</li>
  <li><strong>Logical heading hierarchy</strong> — H2s for main sections, H3s for sub-sections. No skipping levels.</li>
  <li><strong>Content length appropriate</strong> — informational pages should be 1,000+ words; commercial pages 500+ words. Match or exceed the top-ranking competitor.</li>
  <li><strong>LSI keywords used</strong> — related terms and synonyms appear naturally throughout the content.</li>
</ol>

<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551288049-bebda4e38f71?w=900&q=80&fit=crop" alt="Website performance metrics" class="rounded-2xl w-full my-8 shadow-md" loading="lazy" />

<h2>Section 4: Images (3 Points)</h2>

<ol start="14">
  <li><strong>Descriptive file names</strong> — images are named with keywords, not "IMG_4821.jpg". Example: "nairobi-seo-agency.jpg".</li>
  <li><strong>Alt text on every image</strong> — every image has descriptive alt text that includes the keyword where natural.</li>
  <li><strong>Images compressed</strong> — all images are under 200KB. Use WebP format where possible.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Section 5: Links (4 Points)</h2>

<ol start="17">
  <li><strong>Internal links added</strong> — at least 2–3 internal links pointing to relevant pages on your site.</li>
  <li><strong>Anchor text is descriptive</strong> — no "click here" or "read more". Use keyword-rich anchor text like "local SEO services in Nairobi".</li>
  <li><strong>External links open in new tab</strong> — any link leaving your site has target="_blank" and rel="noopener".</li>
  <li><strong>No broken links</strong> — all internal and external links have been checked and are working.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Section 6: Technical On-Page (5 Points)</h2>

<ol start="21">
  <li><strong>Page loads under 3 seconds</strong> — test with Google PageSpeed Insights. A slow page loses rankings and visitors.</li>
  <li><strong>Mobile responsive</strong> — the page looks and functions perfectly on a smartphone.</li>
  <li><strong>Schema markup added</strong> — use appropriate schema (Article, LocalBusiness, FAQ, Product) to help Google understand the page.</li>
  <li><strong>Canonical tag set</strong> — the canonical tag points to the preferred version of the URL.</li>
  <li><strong>Page indexed</strong> — the page is not accidentally blocked by a noindex tag or robots.txt rule.</li>
</ol>

<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1467232004584-a241de8bcf5d?w=900&q=80&fit=crop" alt="Website code and development" class="rounded-2xl w-full my-8 shadow-md" loading="lazy" />

<h2>Quick Reference: On-Page SEO Checklist Summary</h2>

<p>Print this out and use it before publishing every page:</p>

<blockquote>
✅ Primary keyword identified<br/>
✅ Keyword in title tag (near the start)<br/>
✅ Keyword in URL slug<br/>
✅ Keyword in H1<br/>
✅ Keyword in first 100 words<br/>
✅ Title tag 50–60 characters<br/>
✅ Unique title tag<br/>
✅ Meta description 150–160 characters<br/>
✅ No duplicate meta descriptions<br/>
✅ One H1 only<br/>
✅ Logical H2/H3 hierarchy<br/>
✅ Appropriate content length<br/>
✅ LSI keywords used naturally<br/>
✅ Descriptive image file names<br/>
✅ Alt text on every image<br/>
✅ Images compressed under 200KB<br/>
✅ 2–3 internal links added<br/>
✅ Descriptive anchor text<br/>
✅ External links open in new tab<br/>
✅ No broken links<br/>
✅ Page loads under 3 seconds<br/>
✅ Mobile responsive<br/>
✅ Schema markup added<br/>
✅ Canonical tag correct<br/>
✅ Page not blocked from indexing
</blockquote>

<p>Run through this checklist consistently and your pages will be better optimised than 90% of websites in Kenya. SEO rewards consistency above everything else.</p>

